From b1a2cd8c0315f5d87d055b5dcb549aa6d6f95009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deepx-yjsong <yjsong@deepx.ai>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:30:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(msgconv,inputselector,msgbroker): identify the
 source and its capture time in each message

A message says which pad a frame came through, but not which source that is,
which node produced it, or when the frame was captured. With sources added
and removed at runtime, or several nodes publishing to one broker, a
consumer cannot tell messages apart or place them in time.

Source identity
  - dxinputselector sink pads get a "sensor-id" property (mutable in
    PLAYING), set on each frame as DXFrameMeta._sensor_id. Unlike the pad
    index it is not handed to the next source. Set it before linking and
    the first frame carries it.
  - dxmsgconv "node-id" names the producing node.

Capture time
  - dxmsgconv reads the buffer's GstReferenceTimestampMeta, but only the
    wall-clock references: timestamp/x-unix, and timestamp/x-ntp (as rtspsrc
    attaches), converted to the Unix epoch. Other references (e.g. PTP) are
    not UTC and are ignored.
  - The buffer PTS is passed as well.

Message key
  - dxmsgconv sets the source's sensor id as the key on GstDxMsgMeta, and
    the Kafka adapter sends it, so one source's messages stay in order on
    one partition. No sensor id, no key: unchanged round-robin. MQTT
    ignores it.

Wire format
  - dxmsgconv "payload-type" (enum: json, protobuf; default json).
  - dx_msgconvl emits protobuf dxstream.SensorFrame
    (dx_msgconvl/proto/dx_frame.proto), the same fields as the JSON.
    capture_time is a google.protobuf.Timestamp, as in the NVIDIA Metropolis
    schema. No proto3 `optional`, so protoc 3.6+ builds it.
  - New JSON keys (sensorId, nodeId, ptsNs, captureTime) use the proto3 JSON
    names of the same fields; captureTime is RFC 3339 UTC. Existing keys are
    unchanged, and the new ones are omitted when unset.
  - The protobuf backend is optional (-Dprotobuf=auto|enabled|disabled).
    Without it the library builds as before, and protobuf requested at
    runtime fails with an install hint.

Compatibility with existing custom libraries
  - New fields are appended to GstDxMsgMetaInfo and DXFrameMeta, so a
    library built against the old headers still reads its fields at the
    same offsets.
  - DxMsgPayload and DxMsgContext, which libraries allocate, are unchanged.
    The key lives on GstDxMsgMeta, which the element owns.

Tests
  - test_dxmsgconv_identity: sensorId/nodeId, the message key, capture time
    from x-ntp and x-unix, a PTP reference ignored.
  - test_dxinputselector: pad sensor-id stamping.
  - test_dxmsgconv: ptsNs.
  - test_dxframemeta: _sensor_id copy.
  - dx_msgconvl test_protobuf_convert: round trip, with and without times.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
